    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061122.0201\n\nNEW YORK, Nov. 22 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nU.S. stocks open mixed\n\n\n\n\nU.S. stocks opened mixed on Wednesday ahead of the Thanksgiving holiday, as U.S. initial weekly jobless claims rose 12,000 to 321,000.\n\nIn the opening trading, the Dow Jones Industrial Average was down 5.61, to 12,315.98. The Standard  Poor's 500 index gained 0.53 to 1,403.34, and the Nasdaq composite index rose 7.82 to 2,462.66.\n\nInitial claims for state unemployment benefits rose to their highest level since late October, climbing by 12,000 to 321,000, the Labor Department said on Wednesday.\n\nCrude oil prices fell below 60 dollars on Wednesday as concern over supply eased.",
